jobs.description:
**BD & Marketing Executive**
----------------------------

Wedlake Bell is recruiting a BD & Marketing Executive to join our BD & Marketing Team. This is a full-time, permanent role.

Our BD & Marketing team comprises 10 professionals and plays a crucial role in shaping the firm and our future. Our role is to build the firm's reputation among all stakeholders, help develop deeper and broader relationships with our clients and drive future revenue growth. The team consists of:

* BD & Marketing Director;

  + Three Senior BD & Marketing Managers embedded with our practice groups (Private Client, Real Estate, Disputes and Business Services)
  + Senior BD & Marketing Executive
  + BD & Marketing Assistant
* Head of Marketing;

  + CRM Manager
  + Senior Brand & Marketing Executive
  + Events Executive

As a BD & Marketing Executive, your cross-departmental role is critical in both supporting and driving BD & Marketing activities across the firm. Your role will encompass core BD and marketing functions across all legal groups and the firm, providing key support across the team in the development and implementation of marketing & BD plans.

In turn, we offer an unbeatable working culture, a competitive salary and benefits package, and opportunities for your own personal and professional development.

Apply today to find out more.

**About Us:**

Located in the heart of the City of London, Wedlake Bell is a Top 100 law firm offering full services across Private Client, Real Estate, Business Services, and Disputes. The firm has 81 Partners and a total headcount of around 400. We have grown year-on-year, attributed to the continual success of our legal teams, and the dedication of our staff members.

Our culture is widely-recognised as one of the best in City law, built on trust, collaboration, and mutual respect. Joining us, you will be part of a firm which supports work/life balance, personal development, and building strong connections. With regular cross-firm socials and events (including our renowned yearly ski trip and walking trips!), you will quickly feel like part of the Wedlake Bell team.

**Key Responsibilities:**

* Support the BD & Marketing team across all legal groups, sectors and disciplines to create and execute strategic business plans and activities;
* Support on and drive the implementation of BD & Marketing campaigns, considering all elements of the full marketing mix including thought leadership, blogs, social media, webinars, podcasts, events, PR etc;
* Work on pitch and proposal opportunities, delivering strong first-draft documents to the partners and playing an active role in the proposal processes through to completion;
* Support on the pursuit of opportunities to develop new and existing clients as well as suggest ways to cross-sell into the wider Wedlake Bell business;
* Prepare and maintain practice related materials (practice group profiles, deal / matter case studies, thought leadership pieces, CVs, social media posts, client mailings, etc);
* Support on large scale events such as seminars, roundtables, receptions, etc.;
* Source and create relevant content for the firm’s website and intranet;
* Manage and co-ordinate selected legal directory submissions;
* Support with the development and adoption of the firm's CRM system (InterAction);
* Work closely with internal stakeholders to engage with the CRM system to improve communication and knowledge sharing of BD & Marketing opportunities;
* Oversee and run Marketing and BD related reports such as new business, success rates and event attendance and deliverability reports; and
* Other ad hoc duties as required.

**Key Skills and Qualifications:**

* Proven experience as a BD & Marketing Executive in a BD and Marketing function in a partnership environment (law or professional services preferred);
* Ideally, have developed experience using the InterAction CRM, or Vuture (campaign management) – or similar platforms;
* A university degree or equivalent professional qualification in a relevant field (ideally Marketing or Business), or equivalent professional experience;
* Excellent drafting and writing skills – with desirable experience writing copy, creating presentations and other promotional materials – focus on a quality "first-time product" and creativity in approach;
* Excellent interpersonal skills – able to communicate with stakeholders at all levels (both internally and externally);
* Takes a high level of ownership over your workload – able to keep organised, meet deadlines, and demonstrate excellent attention to detail on multiple ongoing projects;
* A proactive and creative approach to problem-solving and suggesting new ideas; and
* Strong IT skills – a good understanding of the MS Office suite, Canva and other relevant programs.

**Why Join Us?**

* A competitive starting salary;
* A comprehensive pension plan;
* 25 days paid holiday per annum, plus additional leave for significant life events;
* Option to purchase up to five additional days of holiday each year;
* Life Assurance and competitive income protection scheme;
* Access to Private Medical and Dental Insurance from day one;
* Enhanced parental leave policies;
* Employee Assistance Programme with face-to-face counselling services;
* Variety of staff wellbeing initiatives including Pilates classes and subsidised gym memberships; and
* A range of bonus schemes recognising referrals and client introductions.

We are dedicated to fostering a diverse and inclusive workplace, where every individual is respected and valued. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates, irrespective of their background or personal circumstances.

If you are passionate about joining a busy team and are eager for a challenging yet fulfilling career, we encourage you to apply.
